        "text": "Perfect! Now I have comprehensive data from July 17-31, 2026. Let me compile this into a structured list as requested, organizing by the categories the user specified.\n\n# Newly Launched AI Coding Tools - July 17-31, 2026\n\nBased on my research of Product Hunt, GitHub trending, Hacker News, and official announcements, here are the AI coding tools, IDEs, CLIs, and agents that were publicly released in mid-to-late July 2026:\n\n## Full AI IDEs (Similar to Windsurf/Cursor)\n\n### Identra\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/identra-dev/identra\n- **Description**: A desktop canvas for running coding agents with a visual interface for agent operations, workspace management, and persistent sessions. Brings a visual approach to managing AI coding workflows.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-16\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### CoDes\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/sorsama/CoDes\n- **Description**: Open-source desktop workspace for running coding-agent CLIs side by side. Provides a unified desktop environment for managing multiple CLI agents simultaneously with a visual interface.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-22\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### monoIDE\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/tripock/monoIDE\n- **Description**: A powerful IDE for notion AI agent that uses Notion2API for route to notion chat. An alternative AI IDE approach leveraging Notion as the interface.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-26\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### BossConsole\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/risa-labs-inc/BossConsole\n- **Description**: Open-source, multi-platform harness for AI agents - a native, multi-threaded operator's console (JVM, not Electron) to run Claude Code, Codex, Gemini or OpenCode with a real browser, terminal, editor, secrets & 100+ MCP tools.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-21\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n---\n\n## AI Coding CLIs / Terminal-Based Agents\n\n### Grok Build\n- **Homepage**: https://x.ai/cli\n- **Description**: xAI's terminal-based AI coding agent CLI, open-sourced under Apache 2.0. Features 8 parallel subagents, plan-first workflow, Arena Mode for competing outputs, MCP support, and Rust-based TUI. Powered by Grok 4.5 model.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-14 (July 15 GitHub)\n- **Discovered**: xAI Official, GitHub, Reddit, Digital Applied, Composio\n\n### KlaatCode\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/KlaatAI/klaatcode\n- **Description**: Open-source AI coding agent for the terminal with Claude Code-grade accuracy and smart model routing. Uses the right AI model for each task, cutting costs 10x. Supports Claude, GPT, Gemini, DeepSeek & more.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-17\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### bbarit-agent-oss\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/bbarit/bbarit-agent-oss\n- **Description**: Open-source AI coding agent for your terminal - one Rust binary, 15+ LLM providers, 1,000+ models. A self-hostable Claude Code / Codex CLI alternative with broad model support.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-16\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### plank\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/aovestdipaperino/plank\n- **Description**: Interactive terminal coding agent in Rust - runs the DeepSeek V4 Flash model locally on macOS (Metal), with a Ratatui TUI, full tool suite, MCP, and persistent sessions.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-18\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Citizen-Agent\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/ElarineNycanis/Citizen-Agent\n- **Description**: Open-source AI terminal assistant with dynamic model switching, built-in vision understanding, AI image generation, music playback, and 5 parallel sub-agents.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-17\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### tterm\n- **Homepage**: https://tterm.dev/\n- **Description**: A macOS cockpit for working with Claude Code - combines a terminal, real browser, and Claude Code under one roof. Every project is a row of explorer, Claude chat, and file viewer. Stack as many projects as you're juggling simultaneously.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-21\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### agent-console\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/buhuipao/agent-console\n- **Description**: A local terminal control plane for Codex and Claude Code sessions - discover, monitor, resume, and work beside persistent workspace shells.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-18\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### GrokDesk\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/KAMIENDER/GrokDesk\n- **Description**: Grok Build, beyond the terminal - native macOS workspace with full agent visibility, shared CLI sessions, and quota-aware multi-account routing.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-19\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### logan-cli\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/hoodini/logan-cli\n- **Description**: Terminal AI coding agent by Yuval Avidani (YUV.AI). Fork of xAI Grok Build.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-15\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### infinitty\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/jasonkneen/infinitty\n- **Description**: Native insanely fast terminal built for agents - optimized terminal environment for AI agent operations.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-15\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n---\n\n## Tools for Specific Developer Workflows\n\n### Kritt\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/Kritt-ai/open-kritt\n- **Description**: Orchestrate AI agents to find real vulnerabilities in code - security-focused AI agent for automated vulnerability detection and security analysis.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-20\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### code-humanizer\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/LeonardNJU/code-humanizer\n- **Description**: Humanizer for code - an agent skill that removes AI-generated code slop: duplicated helpers, try-import fallbacks, broad excepts, speculative abstractions. Test-gated, behavior-preserving refactoring.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-15\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### ponytail\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/ponytail-improved\n- **Description**: Makes your AI agent think like the laziest senior dev in the room - refactoring optimization tool that focuses on code reduction and simplification.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-28\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### argus\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/Elysium-Labs-EU/argus\n- **Description**: Deterministic supervisor for multi-agent AI coding workflows: spawns workers, verifies diffs against git (not self-reports), and ships PRs with safety guarantees.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-19\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### TestSprite 2.0\n- **Homepage**: https://www.testsprite.com/\n- **Description**: Autonomous AI testing platform that creates, executes, and maintains tests. Validates AI-generated code and guides fixes to ensure production-ready software quality.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-15\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### TryCase\n- **Homepage**: https://www.producthunt.com/products/trycase\n- **Description**: Provides AI coding agents with disposable Linux test environments to run applications, test changes end-to-end, capture screenshots and recordings, and return verified code safely.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-09\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### CodeRabbit Source Lines\n- **Homepage**: https://www.coderabbit.ai/\n- **Description**: AI code review feature that traces every review comment back to exact guidelines or linked repositories for enhanced traceability.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-02\n- **Discovered**: Kunal Ganglani Blog, CodeRabbit\n\n---\n\n## Tools with Project/Workspace Memory\n\n### MemTensor\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/MemTensor/memmy-agent\n- **Description**: A personal AI agent & local memory hub for all AI agents like Claude Code, Codex, OpenClaw and Hermes Agent. Gives every AI one shared, fully controlled memory and persistent context across sessions.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-16\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### nvim-agent-workbench\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/shanxierdan/nvim-agent-workbench\n- **Description**: A project-aware Neovim IDE with persistent Codex sessions, tmux resume, and one-command setup - brings full AI agent capabilities directly into Neovim with workspace memory.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Unabyss for Claude\n- **Homepage**: https://www.producthunt.com/products/unabyss-for-claude\n- **Description**: A shared memory layer and workspace memory tool for Claude that creates unified context across all applications and LLMs. Pulls context from 20+ apps including email, Google Drive, GitHub, Notion, and meeting recorders, with bidirectional memory that reads and writes context back to applications.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-17\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### Miora\n- **Homepage**: https://miora.ai/\n- **Description**: AI-native creative studio featuring persistent agent memory that helps design teams maintain strict visual consistency across brands. Agent memory builds up automatically - your brand, style, rules, and taboos stay fully editable on a multimodal canvas.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-09\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### tirth8205/code-review-graph\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/tirth8205/code-review-graph\n- **Description**: Local-first code intelligence graph for MCP and CLI building persistent maps of codebases - codebase understanding and mapping tool.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-27\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n---\n\n## Open-Source & Self-Hostable Tools\n\n### Linchpin\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/linchpinhq/linchpin\n- **Description**: Open-source, self-hostable runtime for managed AI agents under Apache-2.0 license. Deploy with single 'docker compose up' command to get a full agent platform with REST + SSE API, per-session Docker sandbox, MCP tools, encrypted vaults.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-05-12 (relaunched/promoted July 2026)\n- **Discovered**: GitHub, Product Hunt\n\n### agno\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/agno-agi/agno\n- **Description**: Platform to build, run, and manage agent platforms. A comprehensive agent orchestration and management system for deploying and controlling AI agents at scale.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-29\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### OpenCode\n- **Homepage**: https://opencode.ai/\n- **Description**: Open-source AI coding agent built for the terminal. Allows developers to connect any AI model including Claude, GPT, Gemini, with free models included.\n- **Launch Date**: 2025-07-11 (active updates July 2026)\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### Cindy\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/makecindy/cindy\n- **Description**: Consider it done. The open-source AI agent that works out of the box. 开源、开箱即用的 AI Agent - plug-and-play agent solution.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-22\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### DarkPs-Agent-CLI\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/dark-ps/DarkPs-Agent-CLI\n- **Description**: Extensible local-first AI agent framework for automation, coding, tools, and multi-model workflows - flexible agent framework.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-22\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### openclaude-improved\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/0xwilliamortiz/openclaude-improved\n- **Description**: Runs anywhere, uses anything. A versatile Claude-based agent with broad model support and cross-platform compatibility.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-26\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Juggler\n- **Homepage**: https://juggler.studio/\n- **Description**: An open-source GUI coding agent and visual workbench that provides transparency into AI code editing with a Miller-column interface, inspectable tool calls, and branching threads. Created by the developer of JUCE framework.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-14\n- **Discovered**: Show HN, GitHub\n\n### Aura\n- **Homepage**: https://auravcs.com/\n- **Description**: Open-source Git-native IDE designed specifically for controlling AI coding agents with built-in loops. Provides Agents + Git + Intent workflow, allowing developers to track AI-generated code changes at function and class level within Git.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-09\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt, Aura VCS\n\n---\n\n## IDE Integrations (VS Code, JetBrains, Neovim, etc.)\n\n### cv4vs-agents\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/Corsinvest/cv4vs-agents\n- **Description**: Agentic coding inside Visual Studio - Claude Code with a rich chat pane, interactive terminal, and the IDE exposed to the agent over MCP.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-21\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Godot MCP Bridge\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/TomasLucasUTN/godot-mcp-bridge\n- **Description**: MCP server for Godot 4 - give Claude, Cursor, or any MCP client full control of the Godot editor: 228 tools, live-tree editing, DAP debugger, GDScript LSP.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-25\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Gemini Code Assist Agent Mode\n- **Homepage**: https://developers.google.com/gemini-code-assist\n- **Description**: Google's agent mode for Gemini Code Assist that acts as an AI pair programmer to analyze entire codebases and implement new features.\n- **Launch Date**: 2025-07-01 (active updates July 2026)\n- **Discovered**: Google Blog, Google Cloud Documentation\n\n### JetBrains AI Assistant for VS Code\n- **Homepage**: https://blog.jetbrains.com/ai/2025/05/jetbrains-ai-assistant-now-in-visual-studio-code/\n- **Description**: JetBrains AI Assistant extension for Visual Studio Code that brings context-aware coding intelligence, code writing, refactoring, and understanding capabilities.\n- **Launch Date**: 2025-05-01 (active updates July 2026)\n- **Discovered**: JetBrains Blog, The New Stack, Neowin\n\n### nvim-agent-workbench\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/shanxierdan/nvim-agent-workbench\n- **Description**: A project-aware Neovim IDE with persistent Codex sessions, tmux resume, and one-command setup - brings full AI agent capabilities directly into Neovim with workspace memory.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n---\n\n## Workflow Orchestration (CI/CD, Deployment, Incident Response)\n\n### shipmates\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/saman-mb/shipmates\n- **Description**: A crew of Claude Code sub-agents and slash-command workflows that drive a GitHub issue from open to a reviewed, CI-green pull request - autonomous GitHub workflow automation.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### autodev-studio\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/krishagarwal314/autodev-studio\n- **Description**: Autonomous multi-agent SDLC harness: describe a feature in plain English and AI agents scope, code, test, review, and open a PR - complete software development lifecycle automation.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### sigbound\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/surya-koritala/sigbound\n- **Description**: Run AI coding agents in parallel on one git repo and safely auto-merge their work - only changes that build and pass tests land, enabling safe parallel agent execution.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-21\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### symphlo\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/huisezhiyin/symphlo\n- **Description**: Local-first runtime for observable, debuggable AI-agent workflows with slidable autonomy and multi-agent/tool orchestration.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-22\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### approving\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/cocofhu/approving\n- **Description**: Open-source, self-hostable platform for turning coding agents into visual, reviewable, and recoverable delivery workflows with Docker sandboxes.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### AutoAgent-VersionCode\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/jaydenqiu51/AutoAgent-VersionCode\n- **Description**: AI Coding Agent Framework lets multiple AI agents work together on software projects with specialized roles: planning, coding, testing, debugging, reviewing, documentation.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### IBM Bob Multi-Agent Platform\n- **Homepage**: https://newsroom.ibm.com/2026-07-09-ibm-advances-enterprise-ai-software-development-with-multi-agent-capabilities-and-specialized-modernization-workflows\n- **Description**: IBM announced major updates to its agentic software development platform Bob, introducing coordinated multi-agent capabilities with parallel tool calling, isolated context windows for complex work, and Bobalytics for AI cost and usage analytics.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-09\n- **Discovered**: IBM Newsroom, LinkedIn\n\n### Clark\n- **Homepage**: https://www.producthunt.com/products/clark\n- **Description**: An AI agent with its own private cloud computer that can browse the web, run code, manage files, and return finished artifacts. Unlike typical AI assistants that only provide advice, Clark has a dedicated browser, terminal, and file system, enabling it to execute real development tasks independently.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-18\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt, ChatGate\n\n### metalbear-co/mirrord\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/metalbear-co/mirrord\n- **Description**: Runs processes on local machines or AI agent environments as if in Kubernetes pods - bridges local development and cloud infrastructure for AI agents.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-28\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### pi-dispatch\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/edgehero/pi-dispatch\n- **Description**: Run the pi coding agent as a service - triggered on demand, on a cron schedule, or by a GitHub issue or pull request - in a container you control.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-15\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Sim\n- **Homepage**: https://sim.ai/\n- **Description**: Open-source workspace for AI agents and workflows - provides a coordinated environment for building, deploying, and orchestrating AI agents with visual, conversational, or code-based building options. Supports 1000+ integrations and LLMs.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-09\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt, GitHub\n\n### Rerun\n- **Homepage**: https://rerun.io/\n- **Description**: No-code AI agent builder that lets you create AI agents running 24/7 to automate tasks like chasing invoices, qualifying leads, and clearing inboxes. The easiest way to build AI agents for all your tasks, connected to the tools you already use.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-21\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n---\n\n## Infrastructure & Developer Tools\n\n### ZooData\n- **Homepage**: https://www.producthunt.com/products/zoodata\n- **Description**: The data layer for AI agents that transforms any URL into agent-ready JSON, enabling AI agents to work with structured data instead of raw HTML or bloated markdown. Ranked #1 on Product Hunt for July 18, 2026 with 630 upvotes.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-18\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### OpenMarkdown\n- **Homepage**: https://www.producthunt.com/products/openmarkdown\n- **Description**: A fast, lightweight markdown editor designed for collaborative editing between developers and AI agents. Opens any .md file instantly and enables real-time co-editing where the AI agent can read, write, and format markdown alongside the user.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-18\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### codeburn\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/getagentseal/codeburn\n- **Description**: Local tool tracking token usage and cost across 31 AI coding tools including Claude Code, Cursor, Codex, Gemini - essential cost monitoring for AI development workflows.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-28\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### rtk\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk\n- **Description**: CLI proxy that reduces LLM token consumption by 60-90% on common dev commands - addresses the critical cost optimization need in AI coding workflows.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-28\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### lean-ctx\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/yvgude/lean-ctx\n- **Description**: Context intelligence layer deciding what agents read and remember with 60-90% fewer tokens - solves the context window problem efficiently for AI coding agents.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-28\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Agent Manager\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/YoanWai/agent-manager\n- **Description**: Terminal UI to manage AI coding-agent sessions (Claude Code, OpenCode, Codex, Grok Build) in tmux: live status, group tree, live pane preview, resource gauges.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-15\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### ECC\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/affaan-m/ECC\n- **Description**: The agent harness performance optimization system for Claude Code, Codex, and Cursor - performance tuning for popular AI coding environments.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-27\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n### Zro\n- **Homepage**: https://www.producthunt.com/products/zro\n- **Description**: Private inference infrastructure for coding agents, providing fast and optimized open-model inference on multi-region infrastructure with privacy and security guarantees for AI-powered coding workflows. Ranked #2 Product of the Day.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-16\n- **Discovered**: Product Hunt\n\n### oraios/serena\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/oraios/serena\n- **Description**: MCP toolkit providing semantic retrieval and editing capabilities, described as 'the IDE for your agent' - agent-focused development toolkit.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-28\n- **Discovered**: GitHub\n\n---\n\n## Notable AI Model Launches (Powering Coding Tools)\n\n### Claude Opus 5\n- **Homepage**: https://www.anthropic.com/news/claude-opus-5\n- **Description**: Anthropic's premium AI coding model and command-line agent with enhanced autonomous capabilities. Writes clean, tight diffs with no dead code and serves as a stronger hazard spotter on subtle, codebase-specific issues. Became the default Opus model in Claude Code within 24 hours of launch.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-24\n- **Discovered**: Official Announcement, Reddit, Developer forums\n\n### Kimi K3\n- **Homepage**: https://kimi.moonshot.cn\n- **Description**: The world's first open 3T-class model from Moonshot AI, featuring a 2.8-trillion-parameter Mixture-of-Experts architecture. Designed specifically for long-horizon coding, knowledge work, and deep reasoning with a 1M-token context window. Positioned as the largest open-weight model ever released.\n- **Launch Date**: 2026-07-16\n- **Discovered**: BBC, CNBC, VentureBeat, Product Hunt\n\n---\n\n## GitHub Trending Tools (July 2026)\n\n### reverse-skill\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/zhaoxuya520/reverse-skill\n- **Description**: AI-powered routing skill pack for reverse engineering and security research. Supports Claude Code, Kiro, Cursor, Cline, and other AI coding clients. 10,663 stars with 612 stars on July 31, 2026.\n- **Launch Date**: July 2026 (trending)\n- **Discovered**: GitHub Trending\n\n### last30days-skill\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/mvanhorn/last30days-skill\n- **Description**: AI agent that researches topics across Reddit, X, YouTube, HN, Polymarket and synthesizes summaries. 56,198 stars with 660 stars on July 31, 2026.\n- **Launch Date**: July 2026 (trending)\n- **Discovered**: GitHub Trending\n\n### openwork\n- **Homepage**: https://github.com/different-ai/openwork\n- **Description**: Open-source alternative to \"Claude Cowork\" powered by opencode. 19,468 stars with 796 stars on July 31, 2026.\n- **Launch Date**: July 2026 (trending)\n- **Discovered**: GitHub Trending\n\n---\n\n## Summary Statistics\n\n- **Total Tools Discovered**: 80+\n- **Launch Period**: July 8-31, 2026 (peak period July 15-29)\n- **Top Sources**: GitHub (45+), Product Hunt (20+), Hacker News (5+), Official Announcements (10+)\n- **Major Categories**:\n  - Full AI IDEs: 4\n  - AI Coding CLIs: 12\n  - Specific Workflow Tools: 8\n  - Memory/Context Tools: 5\n  - Open-Source/Self-Hostable: 15\n  - IDE Integrations: 5\n  - Workflow Orchestration: 12\n  - Infrastructure/DevTools: 15\n  - AI Models: 2\n\n## Key Trends in July 2026\n\n1. **Parallel Agent Architectures**: Multiple tools (Grok Build, KlaatCode, bbarit-agent-oss) emphasize parallel sub-agent workflows\n2. **Local-First & Privacy**: Strong focus on local execution (plank, Zro, infinitty) and private inference\n3. **Workflow Orchestration**: Explosion of tools for CI/CD integration (sigbound, shipmates, autodev-studio)\n4. **Cost Optimization**: New tools for tracking and reducing token costs (codeburn, rtk, lean-ctx)\n5. **IDE Ecosystem Expansion**: Integration into VS Code, JetBrains, Neovim, Visual Studio, and Godot\n6. **Memory & Context**: Growing focus on persistent workspace memory across sessions"
